---
description: Core workflow rules for the NotebookLM Clone build
alwaysApply: true
---

1. **Work one phase at a time**, in the order defined in §13 of the plan
   (Phase 0 → Phase 5). Do not start a phase until I confirm the previous
   phase's milestone is verified and working.

2. **Context folder**: create a `/context` folder at the project root if it
   doesn't exist. At the end of each phase, create a file named exactly:

   context/Phase{N}\_{ShortName}.md

   matching this convention:
   - context/Phase0_Scaffold_Auth_DB_VectorStore.md
   - context/Phase1_Notebook_Management.md
   - context/Phase2_Ingestion_Pipeline.md
   - context/Phase3_RAG_Query_Pipeline.md
   - context/Phase4_Source_Viewer.md
   - context/Phase5_Polish_Deploy_Submission.md

3. **Each phase's context file must include:**
   - **What was built** — short summary of what this phase delivers
   - **Files created/modified** — list of key paths, with a one-line purpose
     for each
   - **Key decisions & deviations** — anything you implemented differently
     from the plan, and why
   - **Environment variables added/used** — which ones from §11 this phase
     needed
   - **How to verify the milestone** — exact steps to reproduce the
     phase's ✅ milestone from the plan (commands to run, URLs to hit, what
     to check in the DB/Qdrant/UI)
   - **Known issues / TODOs** — anything deferred or incomplete, to carry
     into a later phase
   - **What the next phase needs from this one** — any interfaces, types, or
     setup the next phase will depend on

4. **Before starting any phase**, read all existing files in `/context` first
   so you have full continuity of decisions made in prior phases, even across
   separate sessions.

5. If anything in the project plan is ambiguous or you need to make a
   judgment call not covered by the doc, note the decision in that phase's
   context file rather than silently choosing — I want a record of every
   deviation.

6. Use the tech stack, data model, folder structure, and API design exactly
   as specified in the plan (Next.js 15 App Router, Clerk Google-only auth,
   Prisma + Postgres, Qdrant, BullMQ + Redis, OpenAI embeddings + generation,
   Cohere rerank).
